<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- Made by hand for issue #543 in the way homr 0.7.0 writes a page (as in homr-grace-eighths-4-4): one stream of
     moments over a grand staff, a split moment's left hand written after the right hand's first eighth. homr reads only
     the lower number of a printed time signature and writes the median length of the page's own bars as the upper one;
     it writes a signature only where it sees one printed, and drops one whose lower number is the one already in force.
     Page 1 of 3, printed 4/4: two bars read right, four split (six quarters); homr wrote 5/4. -->
